WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.437
-My first guest is one of the
biggest stars on the planet.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:07.339
His children's book,
"Marcus Makes a Movie,"

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:08.975
is available for preorder.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:11.778
He also is starring in
the Netflix movie "Fatherhood,"

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:14.246
which begins streaming
June 18th.

00:00:14.246 --> 00:00:17.117
Here is the very funny
Kevin Hart!

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.585
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes, my man!

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:21.253
Oh!
Yeah!

00:00:21.253 --> 00:00:24.223
That's what I'm talkin' about.
Ah!

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:27.227
I miss seeing you, bud.
-I know, man.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:30.529
I'm used to walking out there,
high-fiving you, sitting down...

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:32.398
-Right.
-...putting my legs up...

00:00:32.398 --> 00:00:33.666
-Yeah.
-...watching the audience.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.634
There was a thing --
I used to do a thing, man.

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.836
I can't do my thing.
-I know, we had a thing!

00:00:37.836 --> 00:00:39.005
But we can do our thing
in there.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.740
I like your shirt, by the way.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.809
-I don't have on pants.
-No, no, I know!

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.577
I didn't ask that, Kevin.
I did not ask that.

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.679
-I know, but I want you to know,
'cause I'm honest.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:49.048
I don't have on pants.
-I know, but it's not -- no.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.150
You say that every interview.
-Don't ask me to stand up.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.619
-No, I'm not!
Please don't.

00:00:52.619 --> 00:00:54.154
No, no, do not stand up.
Don't encourage him, please.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.487
-All right, I'm gonna do it.
-No, audience!

00:00:55.487 --> 00:00:57.824
-You got the blur button ready?
-No, no, no, no, no!

00:00:57.824 --> 00:01:00.360
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.794
-All right. Okay.
-Don't stand up.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:03.596
-Okay.
All right. Okay.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.698
-I'm gonna need a bigger
thing than that, sorry.

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.033
I'm gonna need, like, a big --
Sorry.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.902
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:11.904
Please don't stand up, bud.
Hey.

00:01:11.904 --> 00:01:13.873
-How you doing?
-I'm doing good, pal.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.975
I do really miss you,
having you here,

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.044
'cause you're always super fun.
I want to talk about --

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.747
You have so many things going
on, so many great projects.

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:23.483
"Marcus Makes a Movie."
But, I want to talk to you --

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:26.519
Since last I talked to you,
you had a baby girl.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.020
Congratulations.
-Yes, man, yes.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.388
-Hey!
-Thank you.

00:01:29.388 --> 00:01:31.824
Thank you.
Another baby.

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.892
Another one.
Father of four now.

00:01:33.892 --> 00:01:35.962
-You guys ready
to see something really cute?

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.263
You ready to see this baby?

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.731
Oh, my God.
Look at this.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:39.899
Kaori.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.000
Look at this.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.503
-Oh, my goodness.

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:45.705
That is --
She looks like a doll.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.473
-Yeah.
My little Cabbage Patch doll.

00:01:47.473 --> 00:01:48.874
-She's so cute.
-My little Cabbage Patch.

00:01:48.874 --> 00:01:50.543
-She really is.
How is it --

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.879
What's it like
having four kids around?

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.713
-Uh, loud.
Very loud.

00:01:54.713 --> 00:01:55.748
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:56.883
-You know?
-A lot of stuff.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.150
-I can't even lie, man.
You know what?

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.286
It's a feeling like no other.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:03.522
I have embraced fatherhood...
-Yeah.

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:06.226
-...you know, with everything
that I have, man.

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:08.294
And, you know,
I got a teenager now.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.895
My oldest is 16.

00:02:09.895 --> 00:02:13.700
My -- My son, Hendrix,
is about to be 14.

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:18.037
My son Kenzo is 3,
and now Kaori, she's 8 months.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:20.039
It's just --
It's insane sometimes

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:23.242
when you are in a home,
and you look around you,

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:25.445
and you look at this --
this thing --

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:28.847
this thing that now exists
that has such a tight

00:02:28.847 --> 00:02:30.283
and close-knit bond, man.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:32.485
And, you know,
I didn't come from

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.487
the mom and dad
in the same household,

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.755
and the family
that ate dinner every night.

00:02:36.755 --> 00:02:39.825
So, the fact that, you know,
I now have broke the --

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:43.563
the mold and created that and
started that, it means a lot.

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:44.897
It means the world to me.
-Yeah, good for you.

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.031
-I love to see it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:46.031 --> 00:02:48.734
Thank you, man.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:52.871
-Your daughter is 16.
And you just --

00:02:52.871 --> 00:02:55.775
She got her driver's license,
and you got her a car.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:02:57.076
-Yeah.
-You bought her a car.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:58.077
Now --
-Yeah.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:00.212
-Did you get a car
when you were 16?

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:01.447
-No, I didn't get no car!

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:02.949
You know damn well
I didn't get no car, Jimmy!

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.117
[ Laughter ]
I didn't get no car.

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:06.785
You want to know what I got?
I got a bucket.

00:03:06.785 --> 00:03:08.888
I got a bucket.
-Oh, you did not get a bucket.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:10.223
Come on.
-Yeah, I got a bucket.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:13.126
I got a bucket,
and in that bucket was nothing.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.395
-There you go.
-If you want something --

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.130
If you want something,
you go do some work

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.198
and fill the bucket up.
That's what I got.

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.567
-So you're saying this kid --
this kid didn't have a car.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.236
He just had a bucket.
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:25.337
-Wow. Wow.
Where'd you get that?

00:03:25.337 --> 00:03:27.106
Hmm?
Jesus Christ.

00:03:27.106 --> 00:03:28.374
I'm sorry.
First of all,

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.276
I want to apologize
to the audience

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.912
for my hairline in that --
in that picture.

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.313
That was a difficult time.

00:03:34.313 --> 00:03:36.148
That's when my mom
was cutting my hair with a bowl.

00:03:36.148 --> 00:03:37.383
True story.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:40.052
She would put a bowl on my head
and go around it.

00:03:40.052 --> 00:03:42.454
But, no, I did not have a car.

00:03:42.454 --> 00:03:45.091
My first car was
a white Trans Am

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.959
that my brother got for me
when I was like --

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:49.428
I think I was like 19.
I didn't get it in high school.

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:51.898
We didn't have cars
in high school...

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:53.332
-No.
-...in Black neighborhoods.

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:55.234
That wasn't a gift.
No, man.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:56.602
-No.
-We had bikes.

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:59.105
Maybe -- Maybe a bike.
And if you rode that to school,

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.940
you weren't coming home with it.
Somebody would steal it.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.674
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:04:02.674 --> 00:04:03.976
-Somebody would steal it.

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:05.911
Let's talk about this.
Can we talk about your book?

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:07.213
Children's book.
-Please do, man.

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:09.348
-This is great, man.
"Marcus Makes a Movie."

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:12.285
I think it's great.
I think it's funny.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.486
It's got a great message
for kids.

00:04:14.486 --> 00:04:16.555
Basically saying,
"Hey, stick with it.

00:04:16.555 --> 00:04:18.157
If you have a dream, work hard.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:19.625
And if you work hard,
you can get somewhere."

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:21.960
-I mean, this is --
this is an opportunity, man,

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:25.998
to really motivate
and inspire our youth.

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:27.900
You know, I feel like
this generation

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.470
needs to truly understand
that the word "no" is just that.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.604
It's a word.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.906
And our stories
are very important.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:37.410
I heard "no" a lot,
you know, on my journey.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.845
And the road to success
is a long one.

00:04:39.845 --> 00:04:42.314
A lot of doors
get closed in your face.

00:04:42.314 --> 00:04:45.451
A lot of roads
have blocks at the end of them,

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.319
and you gotta figure out
ways around them.

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:49.788
And that's what life is about.
It's about pivoting.

00:04:49.788 --> 00:04:52.491
It's about understanding
that your dream is just that.

00:04:52.491 --> 00:04:54.827
It's yours.
And your belief in you

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.196
and your understanding of what
you can do is just that.

00:04:57.196 --> 00:05:01.099
It's yours, and nobody can ever
tell you that that's not true.

00:05:01.099 --> 00:05:03.336
Nobody can ever tell you
that it's not good enough.

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:05.671
In "Marcus Makes a Movie,"
it's about a kid

00:05:05.671 --> 00:05:08.675
that had a dream that --
that kept getting denied.

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:11.511
People kept telling him that
his dream would never happen.

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:14.680
And he was determined
to achieve the goal

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.016
within his dream that he found
a way to do it himself.

00:05:17.016 --> 00:05:19.551
And it became
such an amazing thing for him

00:05:19.551 --> 00:05:21.554
and an amazing thing
for his family

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:24.757
because as he grew
and as he started to understand

00:05:24.757 --> 00:05:27.026
that he was capable of doing
what he put his mind to,

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:29.262
he became a much,
much better individual.

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:31.563
And that's what I want our
generation to understand.

00:05:31.563 --> 00:05:33.299
That's what
I want these kids to understand.

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:35.301
You can be whatever
you want to be in life,

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:37.536
as long as you believe it
and you put your mind to it.

00:05:37.536 --> 00:05:39.739
-That's what I'm talking about.
[ Cheers and applause ]

